{"id": 93899, "acmi_id": "317654", "title": "Public hangings. Series 2. Ep. 01", "title_zh_hans": "", "title_pa": "", "title_hi": "", "title_annotation": "", "title_annotation_zh_hans": "", "title_annotation_pa": "", "title_annotation_hi": "", "slug": "public-hangings-series-2-ep-01", "creator_credit": "Andrew MacKenzie and Lena Corner", "credit_line": "", "credit_line_zh_hans": "", "credit_line_pa": "", "credit_line_hi": "", "headline_credit": "Australia, 2002", "video_links": [], "record_type": "work", "type": "TV show", "is_on_display": false, "last_on_display_place": null, "last_on_display_date": null, "is_context_indigenous": false, "material_description": "", "unpublished": false, "external": false, "first_production_date": "2002-01-01T11:00:00+11:00", "commissioned": false, "public_domain": false, "external_references": [], "brief_description": "<p>Episode number 14 of Series &#8220;Public hangings&#8221;.<br />\nPublic hangings is a local television program on the arts produced for broadcast on community television (channel 31) in Melbourne, Australia from 2002. Enjoying a cult following, the program (now in its second series) produced by Irish art critic and London gallery director, Andrew MacKenzie along with co-presenter Lena Corner, roams the streets of Melbourne in search of opening nights and visual vox pops. The program&#8217;s style makes the avant garde accessible and provides an insight into a vibrant underground city culture. In this episode Andrew MacKenzie introduces a packed program. Tim Danko curates at Westspace &#8220;Paper Skin - Constructed Guts&#8221; an exhibition of the work of thirty contemporary local and overseas comic book producers/artists. Brendan Tolley, Kirrily Schell and Cassandra Tytler are a few of the artists. Nat &amp; Ali provide more comic relief with their lived-in performance on opening night. At Linden St Kilda Contemporary Arts is &#8216;High Tide&#8217;, a photographic exhibition by contemporary indigenous artists looking at the landscape. Curated by Christian Thompson the artists include; Destiny Deacon, Brenda Croft, Michael Riley, Jenny Fraser, Jason Hampton and Dianne Jones. An excerpt of Michael Riley&#8217;s film &#8216;Empire&#8217; is included with music by Anthony Parthos performed by the Tasmanian Symphony Orchestra (first screened on ABC 2000). At Ian Potter Museum of Art &#8216;It&#8217;s a Beautiful Day&#8217; opens. An exhibition exploring the gamut of contemporary painting that includes the work of Peter Booth, Brent Harris, Vivien Shark le Wit, Anne Wallace and David Jolly to name a few. Curated by Bala Starr.</p>", "constellations_primary": [], "constellations_other": [], "recommendations": [], "creator_credit_for_label": "<p>Andrew MacKenzie and Lena Corner</p>", "creator_credit_for_label_zh_hans": "", "creator_credit_for_label_pa": "", "creator_credit_for_label_hi": "", "headline_credit_for_label": "<p>Australia, 2002</p>", "headline_credit_for_label_zh_hans": "", "headline_credit_for_label_pa": "", "headline_credit_for_label_hi": "", "title_for_label_zh_hans": "", "title_for_label_pa": "", "title_for_label_hi": "", "title_for_label_override_zh_hans": "", "title_for_label_override_pa": "", "title_for_label_override_hi": "", "description_for_label_zh_hans": "", "description_for_label_pa": "", "description_for_label_hi": "", "description_for_label_override_zh_hans": "", "description_for_label_override_pa": "", "description_for_label_override_hi": "", "description_zh_hans": "", "description_pa": "", "description_hi": "", "description_override_zh_hans": "", "description_override_pa": "", "description_override_hi": "", "title_for_label": "<p>Public hangings. Series 2. Ep. 01</p>", "description": "<p>Episode number 14 of Series &#8220;Public hangings&#8221;.<br />\nPublic hangings is a local television program on the arts produced for broadcast on community television (channel 31) in Melbourne, Australia from 2002. Enjoying a cult following, the program (now in its